var e=[{slug:`off-grid-gadgets-worth-comparing`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`Off-grid Gadgets Worth Comparing`,summary:`A practical comparison framework for power, water, and lighting tools before you buy anything.`,status:`published`,readTime:`8 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-08-26`,body:[`Most off-grid gear pages compare price, not the numbers that decide whether a tool actually works for your setup. Before you buy anything, you need three figures: real output under load, cycle life, and how the product behaves in the specific climate and use case you have — not the manufacturer's best-case spec sheet.`,`Portable power stations are rated in watt-hours, but usable capacity drops with age, temperature, and inverter efficiency. Ask for the depth-of-discharge figure and the warranty cycle count, not just the headline capacity number. A 500Wh unit rated for 500 cycles at 80% capacity will outlast a 600Wh unit rated for 300 cycles.`,`Gravity water filtration kits live or die on cartridge lifespan and whether replacements are actually stocked where you live. A filter rated for 1,500 gallons sounds generous until you check the flow rate drops off well before that number in real use.`,`Rechargeable area lighting is the easiest category to get right: prioritize a stated lumen-output curve over time, not just a peak-brightness number, and check the IP rating if the light will ever sit outside.`,`We're building comparison tables for each category as we verify real specs and current pricing. Product links go live only after we've confirmed availability and an affiliate relationship exists — nothing here is a paid placement yet.`],productIdeas:[{id:`portable-power-station`,title:`Portable Power Station (Mid-capacity)`,category:`Energy storage`,priceRange:`$300 - $900`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Compare battery chemistry, cycle life, and real output before selecting a unit.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`water-filtration-kit`,title:`Gravity Water Filtration Kit`,category:`Water systems`,priceRange:`$80 - $250`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Shortlist based on filter lifespan and replacement cartridge availability.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`rechargeable-area-light`,title:`Rechargeable Area Light`,category:`Lighting`,priceRange:`$25 - $120`,merchantStatus:`verified`,description:`Prioritize runtime curves, lumen consistency, and weather resistance.`,ctaLabel:`See tested options`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`solar-setups-for-a-small-home`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`Solar Setups for a Small Home`,summary:`A starter guide to sizing panels, batteries, and inverter capacity for everyday needs.`,status:`coming-soon`,readTime:`7 min read`},{slug:`off-grid-home-checklist`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`The Off-grid Home Checklist`,summary:`A decision checklist for shelter, power, water, communications, and backup plans.`,status:`coming-soon`,readTime:`6 min read`},{slug:`tiny-home-technologies-that-make-small-spaces-work`,categorySlug:`tiny-homes`,title:`12 Tiny-Home Technologies That Make Small Spaces Work`,summary:`The systems and fittings that let a small footprint function like a full-size home, not a compromise.`,status:`published`,readTime:`9 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-09-15`,body:[`A tiny home stops feeling small when the systems inside it are chosen for the footprint, not shrunk down from a full-size house. The layouts that work best combine a handful of dual-purpose fittings with a few pieces of technology that quietly do the job of two or three appliances.`,`Start with climate: a single mini-split heat pump sized correctly for the square footage will out-perform a window unit and a space heater combined, and it does it on a fraction of the power draw, which matters if any part of the home runs on stored or solar power.`,`In the kitchen, an induction cooktop paired with compact ventilation frees up the counter and cabinet space a gas range and hood would take, and it runs safely in a space where clearance is tight. Combination washer-dryer units solve the same problem for the utility side of the home.`,`Storage technology matters as much as appliances: hydraulic lift beds, stair-integrated drawers, and fold-flat furniture are the difference between a home that feels cramped and one that feels considered. The best tiny-home builds treat storage as a system to design, not a gap to fill afterward.`,`We're verifying pricing and real-world durability on each category below before linking to specific products. Merchant links go live only once we've confirmed availability and an affiliate relationship exists.`],productIdeas:[{id:`mini-split-heat-pump`,title:`Compact Mini-Split Heat Pump`,category:`Climate control`,priceRange:`$600 - $1,800`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Size against square footage and insulation, not just the marketed room count.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`induction-cooktop`,title:`Two-Burner Induction Cooktop`,category:`Kitchen`,priceRange:`$120 - $350`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Compare wattage draw and pan compatibility before committing to a model.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`hydraulic-lift-bed`,title:`Hydraulic Lift-Storage Bed Frame`,category:`Storage furniture`,priceRange:`$400 - $1,200`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Check lift capacity and mattress-thickness limits against your actual mattress.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`quiet-smart-home-upgrades-worth-trying`,categorySlug:`smart-home`,title:`7 Quiet Smart-Home Upgrades Worth Trying`,summary:`Small, considered automation that lowers a bill or removes a chore without adding a new app to babysit.`,status:`published`,readTime:`7 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-09-15`,body:[`The smart-home upgrades worth having are the ones you stop thinking about within a week. That usually means a small number of well-chosen devices working on a stable local network, not a shelf of gadgets that all want their own app.`,`A smart thermostat with real occupancy sensing pays for itself through the heating and cooling bill alone, and the payback is measurable within a season rather than a guess. Look for local scheduling that still works if the internet connection drops.`,`Energy-monitoring smart plugs on a handful of high-draw devices (the kettle, the dryer, an older fridge) turn a vague utility bill into a number you can act on. This is the cheapest upgrade on the list and the one with the clearest evidence.`,`A video doorbell with local storage avoids the recurring subscription fee that most cloud-only models require, and it solves the actual problem most people buy one for: knowing who is at the door without a subscription.`,`We're testing each category for reliability and total cost of ownership, including subscription fees, before recommending specific models here.`],productIdeas:[{id:`smart-thermostat`,title:`Occupancy-Sensing Smart Thermostat`,category:`Climate control`,priceRange:`$130 - $280`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Confirm local scheduling works without an internet connection before buying.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`energy-monitoring-plug`,title:`Energy-Monitoring Smart Plug (3-pack)`,category:`Energy monitoring`,priceRange:`$35 - $70`,merchantStatus:`verified`,description:`Best entry point — low cost, immediate and measurable bill feedback.`,ctaLabel:`See tested options`,enabled:!1},{id:`video-doorbell-local-storage`,title:`Video Doorbell (Local Storage)`,category:`Home security`,priceRange:`$100 - $220`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Check subscription requirements carefully — many advertised prices exclude storage fees.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`smart-pet-tech-worth-the-money`,categorySlug:`pet-wellness`,title:`Smart Pet Tech Worth the Money`,summary:`A grounded look at GPS trackers, automatic feeders, and air purifiers before you add a pet subscription.`,status:`published`,readTime:`7 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-09-15`,body:[`Pet tech has the same problem as human smart-home gadgets: a lot of it is a subscription wrapped around a sensor. The products worth having are the ones that solve a real daily problem — knowing where a pet is, feeding on schedule when you cannot be home, or keeping shed fur and dander from building up in the air — without locking the core feature behind a monthly fee.`,`GPS trackers vary enormously in real-world range and battery life once you leave a suburban yard for open trail or rural land. Check the actual reported battery life under continuous live-tracking, not the standby figure, and confirm whether the safe-zone alert works without a paid tier.`,`Automatic feeders solve a genuine problem for multi-pet households and irregular schedules, but portion accuracy drifts over time on cheaper units. Look for a mechanism that has a published accuracy tolerance and a hopper that will not jam with the specific food texture you feed.`,`Air purifiers marketed specifically for pet homes mostly differ from general models in filter media tuned for dander and odour rather than raw airflow. The filter replacement cost over a year often matters more than the unit price, so total cost of ownership is the number to compare.`,`We're verifying real battery life, portion accuracy, and filter costs across each category before linking to specific products. Nothing below is a paid placement — merchant links go live only once availability and an affiliate relationship are confirmed.`],productIdeas:[{id:`gps-pet-tracker`,title:`GPS Pet Tracker (No Subscription Required)`,category:`Safety & tracking`,priceRange:`$40 - $100`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Confirm real-world tracking range and safe-zone alerts work without a paid tier.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`automatic-pet-feeder`,title:`Automatic Pet Feeder (Portion-Accurate)`,category:`Feeding`,priceRange:`$60 - $180`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Compare portion accuracy tolerance and hopper jam rate before buying.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`pet-air-purifier`,title:`Pet-Specific Air Purifier`,category:`Air quality`,priceRange:`$120 - $350`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Weigh filter replacement cost per year alongside the upfront unit price.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`bushcraft-timber-frame-shelter-off-grid-basecamp`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`Bushcraft Timber Frame Shelter: Off-Grid Basecamp Guide`,summary:`How to design, cut, and raise a hand-jointed timber frame shelter that holds together through a full season of weather without a tarp.`,status:`published`,readTime:`9 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`A timber frame shelter earns its keep when the joinery is tight enough to shrug off a week of rain without a tarp. The difference between a camp that survives a storm and one that collapses is almost entirely in how the rafter feet land on the top plate and whether the ridge is supported by compression rather than held up by hope.`,`Douglas fir is the most reliable species for hand-cut frames in the Pacific Northwest. It is straight-grained enough to split predictably, stiff enough to resist rafter sag on spans up to four metres, and available in the 150mm x 150mm section that makes corner joinery manageable with hand tools. Avoid green timber for structural members — it will check and loosen every joint as it dries.`,`The birds-mouth rafter cut is the single most important joint in the whole frame. Cut it so the seat depth is exactly one-third of the rafter depth, no more — a deeper cut removes too much material and weakens the rafter at the point of highest bending stress. A well-cut birds-mouth sits flat on the top plate with no rocking and no daylight at the back of the notch.`,`For a basecamp shelter intended to stay in place, set the sill on a stone-and-timber pad elevated at least 150mm above the surrounding ground. This keeps the sill dry through snowmelt and stops rot starting at the base of the posts where moisture sits longest. Flat river stones and short cedar offcuts work well and require no concrete.`,`Power needs at a basecamp are modest but real: a reading light, a water pump, and a phone charger cover most situations. A compact EcoFlow Delta Pro 2 on a rough timber shelf inside the frame, charged from a single panel bolted to the south-facing rafter, handles all three on a full charge through a typical overcast week.`],productIdeas:[{id:`portable-power-basecamp`,title:`Portable Power Station (Basecamp)`,category:`Energy storage`,priceRange:`$500 - $1,200`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Size against your actual load: lighting, pump, and phone charging.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`compact-solar-panel-rafter`,title:`Compact Folding Solar Panel (100–200W)`,category:`Solar`,priceRange:`$120 - $350`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Check real output under partial cloud, not peak-spec wattage.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`underground-rainwater-cistern-off-grid-water`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`Underground Rainwater Cistern: Off-Grid Water System Guide`,summary:`How to size, bury, and plumb a rainwater cistern that supplies reliable household pressure from a steel roof and a 12V pump.`,status:`published`,readTime:`8 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`A buried cistern is the most reliable water supply a homestead can have once it is sized correctly and the collection surface is clean. Unlike a tank above grade, a buried cistern stays at near-constant temperature, eliminating algae growth in summer and freeze risk in winter, and it removes the visual footprint from the yard entirely.`,`Sizing starts with the roof collection area and the local rainfall pattern, not a round number. Multiply the roof area in square metres by average monthly rainfall in millimetres, apply a 0.85 coefficient for real-world losses from splashing and gutter waste, and that gives you the litres you can realistically collect per month. Your storage volume should cover your household demand through the longest typical dry spell in your region, plus a 20% buffer.`,`Precast concrete cisterns are the most durable option for permanent installations. They resist UV, do not leach chemicals, and last for decades without maintenance beyond annual inspection. The main cost is delivery — precast units are heavy — so access for a flatbed and crane is a planning requirement before you choose a location.`,`First-flush diverters are non-negotiable on any food or drinking supply. The first 25 litres of runoff from a dry roof carries bird droppings, leaf debris, and accumulated dust. A correctly sized diverter shunts this to ground before the cistern inlet opens. A UV filter at the inlet, not just at the tap, kills any pathogens that make it past the diverter.`,`A 12V DC pump powered by a portable power station keeps the whole system independent of the grid and draws far less than a mains-pressure pump. Set a float valve at the cistern to control overflow to a downhill swale, and the system runs without daily attention once the initial sizing is right.`],productIdeas:[{id:`12v-water-pump`,title:`12V DC Pressure Water Pump`,category:`Water systems`,priceRange:`$60 - $180`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Check pressure rating and flow rate against your pipe diameter and head height.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`first-flush-diverter`,title:`First-Flush Diverter Kit`,category:`Water systems`,priceRange:`$45 - $120`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Size the chamber volume to at least 1L per 25sqm of roof area.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`shipping-container-pool-deck-off-grid-backyard`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`Shipping Container Pool: Off-Grid Backyard Build Guide`,summary:`How to convert a 40-foot high-cube container into a partially in-ground pool with a timber deck and solar-powered pump system.`,status:`published`,readTime:`10 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`A decommissioned shipping container makes a structurally sound pool shell once the cut openings are reinforced and the interior is coated correctly. The steel structure, designed to stack six units high at sea, is massively overbuilt for a static in-ground application, which is what makes it structurally viable in the first place.`,`The critical step is the cut opening. Shipping containers derive their rigidity from the corrugated side panels — cut an opening without adding a steel frame header and the container will distort under load within a season. Before any cutting, weld a 100mm x 100mm RHS steel frame around the entire planned opening. This transfers the load path around the cut and keeps the container square.`,`The interior coating must be a marine-grade liner, not a painted surface. Paint lifts within a season when submerged. A spray-applied polyurea liner or a fitted vinyl liner anchored at the lip are the two options that hold long-term. Budget the liner as a significant fraction of the total project cost — it is not a place to economise.`,`Partial in-ground placement solves two problems: it reduces the visible height of the container above grade and it uses the surrounding soil as thermal mass to moderate water temperature. Excavate so the container sits with its floor at least 600mm below grade on the long sides, while the cut opening side remains accessible at deck level.`,`Power for the pump and lighting comes cleanly from a solar-charged portable power station inside the container. An EcoFlow Delta Pro 2 in a ventilated internal compartment, charged by a panel on the container roof, handles the circulation pump, LED strip lighting under the deck lip, and an outdoor shower without a grid connection.`],productIdeas:[{id:`pool-circulation-pump`,title:`Low-Watt Pool Circulation Pump`,category:`Water systems`,priceRange:`$150 - $400`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Size to the container volume and match the wattage to your power station capacity.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`ipe-decking-timber`,title:`Ipe Hardwood Decking Timber`,category:`Decking`,priceRange:`$80 - $180 per sqm`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Verify moisture content and confirm the supplier holds FSC certification.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`rammed-earth-passive-solar-studio-off-grid`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`Rammed Earth Passive Solar Studio: Off-Grid Build Guide`,summary:`How a 600mm rammed earth wall paired with clerestory glazing eliminates heating and cooling costs in a dry climate studio.`,status:`published`,readTime:`9 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`A rammed earth wall is not just a material choice — it is a thermal strategy. The dense compacted soil absorbs heat during the day and releases it slowly through the night, acting as a battery that smooths out temperature swings without mechanical assistance. In a dry climate with a large diurnal temperature range, that behaviour eliminates air conditioning and dramatically reduces heating loads.`,`The wall thickness that delivers useful thermal mass is 500–600mm. Below that, the wall still works structurally but loses most of its time-lag benefit — the heat moves through too quickly to buffer overnight temperatures effectively. Above 700mm, the cost of the additional material and formwork rarely pays back in energy savings.`,`Clerestory glazing on the north face (southern hemisphere) or south face (northern hemisphere) brings diffused light deep into the plan without the solar gain that south-facing glass generates in summer. A 400mm roof overhang calculated to the local sun angle shades the glass completely at midsummer noon but allows full winter sun penetration when the angle is low.`,`Passive solar design only works if the thermal mass is in direct contact with the sunlight path. A rammed earth wall behind glass on the sun-facing elevation — a Trombe wall configuration — collects heat directly and releases it to the interior overnight. A polished concrete floor on a sand-and-gravel sub-base adds a second thermal layer that costs almost nothing extra once the slab is already being poured.`,`Roof-mounted solar on a passive-designed studio is genuinely efficient because the base load is so low. An EcoFlow Pro system handling lighting, a computer, and a small appliance or two typically draws well under 3kWh per day from a correctly insulated passive building, making a modest roof array sufficient for year-round power independence.`],productIdeas:[{id:`rammed-earth-formwork`,title:`Adjustable Steel Rammed Earth Formwork`,category:`Construction`,priceRange:`$800 - $2,500`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Verify panel width matches your planned wall thickness before ordering.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`solar-power-station-studio`,title:`Solar Power Station (Studio Load)`,category:`Energy storage`,priceRange:`$600 - $1,500`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Measure actual daily draw before sizing — passive buildings use far less than assumed.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`micro-hydro-creek-power-off-grid-energy`,categorySlug:`off-grid`,title:`Micro Hydro Creek Power: Off-Grid Energy System Guide`,summary:`How a small year-round creek, a penstock pipe, and a Pelton turbine produce consistent household power regardless of cloud cover or season.`,status:`published`,readTime:`8 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`A small year-round creek is the most reliable power source a rural property can have. Unlike solar, it produces consistent watts regardless of cloud cover. Unlike wind, it does not require a tower or a large cleared area. If the property has a creek with sufficient flow and head — the vertical drop between intake and turbine — micro hydro is almost always the most cost-effective off-grid energy source available.`,`Head is the primary driver of output. A 2-inch penstock running 80 vertical feet of head will produce meaningful power from a modest flow rate. The basic calculation: head in metres multiplied by flow in litres per second multiplied by 5.6 gives a rough output in watts for a well-matched Pelton turbine. Calculate your available head and flow before selecting any other component.`,`The rock-box intake is a simple but critical piece of engineering. It is a small stone-lined pool at the creek diversion point, sized so the water slows enough for sediment to drop out before entering the penstock pipe. Without it, fine grit carried in creek water will erode the turbine nozzle and runner within a season.`,`A Pelton turbine is the right choice for high-head, low-flow applications — the most common configuration on small rural properties. The runner cups are replaceable, which matters because any grit that makes it through the intake will eventually wear them. Turbine manufacturers should be able to quote expected cup life at your flow velocity.`,`The battery management layer makes the difference between a system that works and one that needs constant attention. An EcoFlow Pro 3 with its charge controller integration manages the battery bank, handles load switching, and provides a status display that makes it easy to confirm the system is operating within normal parameters at a glance.`],productIdeas:[{id:`pelton-turbine`,title:`Pelton Turbine (100–500W)`,category:`Hydro power`,priceRange:`$400 - $1,800`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Match nozzle size to your calculated flow rate for best efficiency.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`hdpe-penstock-pipe`,title:`HDPE Penstock Pipe (2–4 inch)`,category:`Hydro power`,priceRange:`$3 - $12 per metre`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Use PN10 or higher pressure rating — undersized pipe bursts under operating head.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`smoked-glass-cloche-halloween-centrepiece`,categorySlug:`halloween`,title:`Smoked Glass Cloche Centrepiece: Modern Halloween Table Styling`,summary:`How to arrange three smoked-glass cloches with dried botanicals and under-lighting into a Halloween centrepiece that holds for the full month.`,status:`published`,readTime:`6 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`The strongest seasonal styling works because it uses a clear material story rather than a pile of novelty objects. Three smoked-glass cloches in descending heights, each holding a single dried botanical, lit from below — that is a complete and considered piece. Nothing else needs to go on the runner.`,`Smoked glass is the right choice for Halloween because it keeps the interior visible but softened. A dried honesty stem, a skeletal umbelifer, or a small branch of dried Chinese lantern plant inside a smoked cloche looks rare and deliberate rather than decorative. The glass does the work that elaborate staging would otherwise need to do.`,`Height variation is what makes the grouping read as collected rather than bought as a set. The tallest cloche should be roughly twice the height of the shortest. Place the tallest off-centre, set the smallest at the opposite end of the grouping, and let the middle height sit between them. The arrangement should look like three related objects, not a matched set.`,`The LED underlighting is the detail that lifts the whole piece at dusk. A thin disc of warm white LED — 2700K colour temperature, not cool daylight — placed under each cloche base creates a glow that reads through the smoked glass without burning out the botanical silhouette inside. Battery-operated puck lights work perfectly and require no wiring.`,`The palette that holds this together for the full month: aged brass, deep charcoal, warm ivory, and dusty sage. Those four tones work in both daylight and lamplight, and they do not lock the centrepiece into Halloween-only territory — the piece can sit on the table from mid-October through to early November without looking dated.`],productIdeas:[{id:`smoked-glass-cloches`,title:`Smoked Glass Cloches (Set of 3, Mixed Heights)`,category:`Table styling`,priceRange:`$45 - $120`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Confirm the base diameter before buying — LED puck lights need 5cm clearance underneath.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`warm-led-puck-lights`,title:`Battery LED Puck Lights (Warm White 2700K)`,category:`Lighting`,priceRange:`$18 - $45`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Check the colour temperature — cool daylight kills the effect entirely.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`dried-wheat-sheaf-front-door-wreath-autumn-halloween`,categorySlug:`halloween`,title:`Dried Wheat Sheaf Wreath: Autumn Front Door Styling Guide`,summary:`How to bind, layer, and hang a dried wheat sheaf wreath that works from September through November without looking dated.`,status:`published`,readTime:`6 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`A wheat sheaf wreath works from mid-September through to November without looking dated because it anchors in harvest rather than in specific Halloween imagery. It earns its place on the door for six weeks rather than ten days, which justifies the time spent making it properly.`,`Bind the wheat into a generous flat-backed sheaf first, not a circular wreath. A flat-backed shape hangs flush against a door, reads better in photographs, and is easier to build with a tight, symmetrical result. Use natural jute twine at three binding points: low on the stems, at mid-shaft, and just below the ears. Each binding should be tight enough that no individual stem shifts when the door moves.`,`The floral accent goes at the top, placed after binding. Two or three stems of dried burgundy dahlias pressed into the ears of wheat, or a small bundle of dried pampas at the crown, is enough. More than that and the piece starts to compete with itself. The wheat should still be the primary material when someone looks at the door from the street.`,`The ribbon is a design decision, not an afterthought. Wide natural linen ribbon — at least 80mm wide — folded into a simple bow at the lower binding point creates a weight at the base that balances the visual mass of the ears at the top. Satin or synthetic ribbon at any width makes the same piece look cheap instantly.`,`Hang the wreath at eye height, not door-top height. The texture and construction of a well-made sheaf wreath registers at close range — ear shape, binding pattern, the individual stem ends — and all of that is invisible if the wreath sits three metres off the ground. Eye height also photographs correctly in natural light without requiring a step ladder.`],productIdeas:[{id:`dried-wheat-sheaf-bundle`,title:`Dried Wheat Sheaf Bundle (Natural)`,category:`Seasonal decor`,priceRange:`$15 - $45`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Buy enough for two rounds — the first practice binding teaches you what you actually need.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1},{id:`wide-linen-ribbon`,title:`Wide Natural Linen Ribbon (80mm+)`,category:`Styling materials`,priceRange:`$8 - $22`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Confirm it is linen or cotton, not polyester — polyester catches light differently and looks wrong.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`dark-velvet-pumpkin-cluster-luxury-halloween-entry-table`,categorySlug:`halloween`,title:`Dark Velvet Pumpkin Cluster: Luxury Halloween Entry Table`,summary:`How to style a marble entry table with velvet pumpkins and a single black candlestick into a Halloween display that reads as collected, not decorated.`,status:`published`,readTime:`5 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-07`,body:[`Velvet pumpkins in a tight cluster read as deliberately collected rather than decorated, especially when the colours are all from the same dark family rather than contrasting bright and dark. This is the single most important principle behind the whole approach: colour consistency is what separates a considered grouping from a jumble.`,`Seven pumpkins is the right number for a standard entry table. Fewer than five and the cluster lacks visual weight. More than nine and the table starts to look like a shop display. Group them by size rather than by colour — three large at the back, two medium in the middle, two small at the front — and allow them to touch each other. No gaps.`,`The colour range is black, deep plum, and midnight navy. All three read as near-black at a distance, which keeps the grouping tight, but each colour has enough distinction to reward closer inspection. Avoid any pumpkin that has a highlight colour — ochre stem, orange stitching — that pulls the eye away from the velvet surface.`,`A single tall black candlestick at the back of the grouping provides the vertical element that anchors the whole table. Without it, the pumpkin cluster sits flat and small on a large table surface. With it, the arrangement has a clear hierarchy — tall back, tight cluster foreground — that reads as composed rather than placed.`,`The rest of the table should be empty. A marble entry table with a dark velvet pumpkin cluster and a single candlestick, nothing else, is a complete and confident piece. Adding a tray, a runner, or extra candles dilutes the effect immediately. The empty marble surface is as much a part of the design as the objects on it.`],productIdeas:[{id:`velvet-pumpkins-dark`,title:`Velvet Pumpkins (Dark Tones, Set of 7)`,category:`Seasonal decor`,priceRange:`$55 - $140`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Order all from the same maker — dye lots vary significantly between suppliers.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`tall-black-candlestick`,title:`Tall Black Candlestick (400mm+)`,category:`Table styling`,priceRange:`$25 - $70`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Matte finish only — gloss black competes with the velvet surface.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]},{slug:`maine-coon-indoor-luxury-glass-cabin-guide`,categorySlug:`pet-wellness`,title:`Maine Coon at Home: Indoor Luxury and Glass Architecture`,summary:`Understanding the Maine Coon's scale, coat, and temperament — and how modern glass architecture creates the perfect environment for the breed.`,status:`published`,readTime:`7 min read`,lastUpdated:`2026-10-06`,body:[`The Maine Coon is the largest domestic cat breed, with a dense lion-like ruff, long tufted paws, and a bushy tail nearly as long as its body. At full adult size — typically 5 to 8kg for females, 7 to 12kg for males — a Maine Coon occupies a room differently from most cats. It is not a lap cat in the usual sense. It is a presence.`,`The breed's double-layer coat is engineered for cold. The dense undercoat insulates, the silky guard hairs shed water and light, and the ear furnishings and paw tufts are specific adaptations for deep snow. In a modern heated interior, that coat requires weekly combing at minimum — more during the spring moult — to prevent matting at the ruff and behind the elbows where the layers compress most.`,`Maine Coons are unusually comfortable with glass walls and large open spaces. Unlike more anxious breeds that retreat from wide-open views, the Maine Coon tends to position itself in the most exposed vantage point in a room and watch what is happening outside for extended periods. A wide window ledge in a glass-walled cabin is not an unusual environment for the breed — it is exactly where they choose to be.`,`The breed is gregarious and vocal in a chirping rather than yowling register. They adapt well to households with other animals and do not require the constant engagement that some active breeds demand. A Maine Coon in a quiet woodland cabin, given a high ledge, a window, and a weekly groom, is a settled and content animal.`,`For indoor enrichment, the Maine Coon needs vertical space more than floor space. A floor-to-ceiling cat tree or a shelf system at two or three heights satisfies their instinct to observe from elevation without requiring outdoor access. The breed is large enough that cheap cat furniture fails structurally within a season — budget for solid timber or welded steel frames.`],productIdeas:[{id:`large-breed-cat-tree`,title:`Solid-Frame Cat Tree (Large Breed)`,category:`Cat furniture`,priceRange:`$150 - $450`,merchantStatus:`shortlisted`,description:`Confirm the base weight and bolting point — large cats tip lightweight trees.`,ctaLabel:`Price check`,enabled:!1},{id:`deshedding-grooming-tool`,title:`De-Shedding Grooming Rake (Long Hair)`,category:`Grooming`,priceRange:`$25 - $65`,merchantStatus:`unverified`,description:`Maine Coon coats need a rake, not a slicker brush — the undercoat mats at root level.`,ctaLabel:`Merchant pending`,enabled:!1}]}];function t(){return e}function n(t){return e.find(e=>e.slug===t)}function r(t){return e.filter(e=>e.categorySlug===t)}export{t as n,r,n as t};